course: dictionary
lesson: 9763
title: Suppose: think, imagine, or should
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word suppose has a few meanings, and the words around it tell you which one. Suppose can mean to think something might be true, or to guess it. «I suppose you want to go off in a coach-and-four!» The speaker is guessing what someone wants, not saying it for certain.
explain: Suppose can also mean to imagine a case, like a what-if. «Suppose each box holds 6 eggs» means: pretend this is true, then work out the answer. In maths, this is how you start an if-case to work with.
explain: Be supposed to is a different meaning. It means should, or be planned to. «In a rented home, the landlord is supposed to fix the damp» means it is the landlord's job to fix it. The verb changes its form here: suppose becomes supposed.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence. If guess, think or imagine fits, you have the right meaning. For supposed to, try should. If should fits, you have it.
fact: Suppose is a verb: suppose, supposes, supposed, supposing.
fact: «Suppose» can mean think or guess, as in «I suppose so».
fact: «Suppose» can mean imagine, as in «suppose you had a million dollars».
fact: «Be supposed to» means should, or be planned to: «you are supposed to wear a hat».
fact: «Supposed to» can also mean people say it is so: «the film is supposed to be good».
exercise: «I suppose you want to go off in a coach-and-four!» What does suppose mean here? | To buy something expensive | *To guess or think something is likely | To close a door | To run very fast
exercise: «You are supposed to wear a hat in the sun.» What does supposed to mean here? | Very much liked | Must never | *Should, or are planned to | Forgotten
exercise: «Suppose each box holds 6 eggs. How many eggs are in 3 boxes?» What does suppose mean here? | Forget the answer | Count the eggs in the shop | Break the boxes open | *Imagine a case to work with
test: «The film is supposed to be good.» What does supposed to mean here? | It has been lost | *People say it is good | It is definitely the best film ever made | Someone is hiding it
test: Mia says, «I suppose so», when asked if it will rain. What does she mean? | I know for certain it will rain | I do not want to answer | It is raining now | *I think so, probably
exam: Which sentence uses suppose to mean imagine a case? | «The film is supposed to be good.» | «You are supposed to wear a hat.» | «I suppose so.» | *«Suppose you had a million dollars.»
